  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A match between Mary and Bob consists of successive rounds where each round has exactly one winner. Play stops as soon as a player has won five rounds. How many distinct sequences of round results can the match have if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q17-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Mary didn’t win any rounds?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$. Bob wins five rounds in a row.",
          "worked": "The only sequence is BBBBB, where B denotes a round won by Bob. There is $1$ sequence.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q17-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Mary won exactly one round?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5$",
          "worked": "Bob wins the final round. Before it, arrange four B’s and one M, where M denotes a round won by Mary.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{5!}{4!}\\\\N&=5.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q17-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Mary won exactly two rounds?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15$",
          "worked": "Bob wins the final round. Before it, arrange four B’s and two M’s.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{6!}{4!\\,2!}\\\\N&=15.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q17-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Mary won exactly three rounds?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$35$",
          "worked": "Bob wins the final round. Before it, arrange four B’s and three M’s.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{7!}{4!\\,3!}\\\\N&=35.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q17-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Mary won exactly four rounds?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$70$",
          "worked": "Bob wins the final round. Before it, arrange four B’s and four M’s.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{8!}{4!\\,4!}\\\\N&=70.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q17-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Mary won five rounds and is declared the winner?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$126$\n\nBy symmetry, add the counts in parts (a)–(e).",
          "worked": "Swapping Mary’s and Bob’s names pairs each match won by Bob with one won by Mary. Parts (a)–(e) count all matches won by Bob.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=1+5+15+35+70\\\\N&=126.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
